# INV-12 — invented. Four overs a side: the wicket-keeper.
# Edge cases: the gloves named at the start (kp:F1), changed mid-over when the
# keeper is hurt (kp:F2, the bowler bowling on) and given back (kp:F1 again:
# the same line on the card, F1 and F2 in the order they first kept); a
# catch credited to the keeper by his number (a catch by F5 is no keeper's);
# stumpings credited to whoever keeps at the time, one off a wide (the
# bowler's wicket, no ball of the over: falls at 1.4); a catch by the keeper
# off a free hit saved, which is no wicket and no keeper's catch; a run out
# by the keeper, which is neither a catch nor a stumping; five penalty runs
# to the batting side for the keeper's unfair movement (in its total, none
# the bowler's) and five for a fielder's; a maiden with three wickets; a
# chase lost by one run.
